Possible problems: 1. The output current is too large;
2. The hall or detection circuit is disturbed or abnormal;
3. Hall is disconnected or abnormal;
4. Abnormal rotation signal. 1. The output current is too large. 2. The Hall or Detection Circuit is abnormal. 3. The Hall is disconnected or abnormal. 4. The resolver signal is abnormal. || Corrective action: check if the motor is out of control;
Check whether the load is too large to cause the motor output current to be too large;
Check the VCU torque request instructions;
Check whether the three-phase output cable is damaged;
