troubleshoot_en:
Step 1. Unplug the ECU's 15-hole plug and measure whether the 15P-15 and 15P-4 or power lines are short circuited; if there is a short circuit, go to step 2; if not, go to step 4;
Step 2. Unplug the wiring plug of the front axle solenoid valve and measure the voltage at 1 pin of the plug. If it is not about 0V, repair the wiring harness; if the voltage is about 0V, go to step 3;
Step 3. Measure the voltage at 1 pin of the front axle solenoid valve socket. If it is not about 0V, replace the solenoid valve; if it is about 0V, go to step 4;
Step 4. Restore all plug-in states, replace the ECU, and recalibrate the ECAS. ; Action: Line maintenance correction

Step 1. Unplug the ECU's 15-hole plug and measure the resistance between 15P-15 and 15P-4; if it's infinite, go to step 2; if it's about 78 ohms, go to step 4;
Step 2. Measure the resistance between pin 1 and 4 of the front axle solenoid valve socket. If it is infinite, replace the solenoid valve; if it is about 78 Euros, go to step 3;
Step 3. Measure the wiring plug of the front axle solenoid valve, measure whether pin 1 of the plug is connected to the 15P-15 of the ECU. If not, repair the wiring harness; if it is conductive, go to step 4;
Step 4. Restore all plug-in states, restart the power supply, and if the fault persists, replace the ECU and re-calibrate the ECAS. ; Action: Line maintenance correction

Step 1. Unplug the ECU's 15-hole plug and measure whether the 15P-15 and ground wire are short circuited; if there is a short circuit, go to step 2; if not, go to step 4;
Step 2. Unplug the wiring plug of the front axle solenoid valve and measure whether pin 1 of the plug and the ground wire are short circuited. If there is a short circuit, repair the wiring harness; if there is no short circuit, go to step 3;
Step 3. Measure whether pin 1 of the front axle solenoid valve socket is short circuited. If there is a short circuit, replace the solenoid valve; if not, go to step 4;
Step 4. Restore all plug-in states, replace the ECU, and recalibrate the ECAS. ; Action: Line maintenance correction

Step 1. Unplug the ECU's 15-hole plug and measure whether the 15P-13 and 15P-4 or power lines are short circuited; if there is a short circuit, go to step 2; if not, go to step 4;
Step 2. Unplug the wiring plug of the rear axle solenoid valve and measure the voltage on the 2 pins of the plug. If it is not about 0V, repair the wiring harness; if the voltage is about 0V, go to step 3;
Step 3. Measure the 2-pin voltage of the rear axle solenoid valve socket. If it is not about 0V, replace the solenoid valve; if it is around 0V, go to step 4;
Step 4. Restore all plug-in states, replace the ECU, and recalibrate the ECAS. ; Action: Line maintenance correction

Step 1. Unplug the ECU's 15-hole plug and measure the resistance between 15P-13 and 15P-4; if it's infinite, go to step 2; if it's about 78 ohms, go to step 4;
Step 2. Measure the resistance between pins 2 and 4 of the rear axle solenoid valve socket. If it is infinite, replace the solenoid valve; if it is around 78 Euros, go to step 3;
Step 3. Measure the wiring plug of the rear axle solenoid valve, measure whether the 2 pins of the plug are connected to the 15P-13 of the ECU. If not, repair the wiring harness; if it is conductive, go to step 4;
Step 4. Restore all plug-in states, restart the power supply, and if the fault persists, replace the ECU and re-calibrate the ECAS. ; Action: Line maintenance correction

