Step 1. Unplug the 15-hole plug of the ECU wiring harness, measure the resistance between 15P-9 and 15P-7, check that the sensor resistance should be about 122 ohms to rule out multimeter errors, if the resistance gap exceeds
After 7 Euros, check the wiring harness or replace the sensor; if the resistance is normal, go to step 2;
Step 2. Through the diagnostic equipment, check the ECU parameter settings and confirm that the height sensor type is selected correctly. If the parameters are set correctly, replace the ECU and re-calibrate the ECAS. ; Action: Line maintenance correction

