trigger_en:
Entry conditions: PowerON, SJB power supply, PWM output | Mature conditions: Battery thermal management three-way valve failure:
① VDC has not received feedback from the three-way valve. The compressor, fan and WPTC are prohibited from working, and the three-way battery valve is faulty. When the battery thermal management is in non-cooling mode, fault level 1; when in cooling or heating mode, fault level 2;

② When the three-way valve is blocked, 0x32 is generated on both sides. If there is no feedback failure, the maximum speed of the compressor on both sides is limited to 4000 rpm, the maximum power of the WPTC is 10 kW, fault level 1. If there is still fault feedback, the compressor, fan and WPTC are prohibited from working, and the battery three-way valve is reported. When the battery thermal management is in uncooled mode, fault level 1; when in cooling or heating mode, fault level 2;

③ When the three-way valve reports other faults other than blocking rotation, the compressor, fan, and WPTC are prohibited from working, and the three-way battery valve failure is reported. When the battery thermal management is not in cooling mode, fault level 1; when in cooling or heating mode, fault level 2. | Diagnosis Cycle (ms): 10000

Entry conditions: PowerON, SJB power supply | Mature conditions: Battery thermal management three-way valve failure:
① VDC has not received feedback from the three-way valve. The compressor, fan and WPTC are prohibited from working, and the three-way battery valve is faulty. When the battery thermal management is in non-cooling mode, fault level 1; when in cooling or heating mode, fault level 2;

② When the three-way valve is blocked, 0x32 is generated on both sides. If there is no feedback failure, the maximum speed of the compressor on both sides is limited to 4000 rpm, the maximum power of the WPTC is 10 kW, fault level 1. If there is still fault feedback, the compressor, fan and WPTC are prohibited from working, and the battery three-way valve is reported. When the battery thermal management is in uncooled mode, fault level 1; when in cooling or heating mode, fault level 2;

③ When the three-way valve reports other faults other than blocking rotation, the compressor, fan, and WPTC are prohibited from working, and the three-way battery valve failure is reported. When the battery thermal management is not in cooling mode, fault level 1; when in cooling or heating mode, fault level 2. | Diagnosis Cycle (ms): 10000

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (6s)
Adhesion detection command:
(1) Adhesion detection enabled;
(2) The main circuit has no internal network failure;
(3) The contactor has no adhesion failure;
(4) The circuit state machine is ready to precharge the power state or to control the power state when ready
 Perform an adhesion test if the above conditions are met

Reset conditions:
(1) Faults cannot be automatically recovered.
(2) If the power is turned on again and the fault entry conditions are not met, the fault will exit.

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (2ms)
(1) The power-on state is ready to be powered on (state 1);
(2) The back-end voltage of the contactor is greater than 15V;
(1) AND (2) 

Reset conditions:
(1) The power-on state is not ready to be powered on (state 1);
(2) The original power-up instructions are invalid;
(3) When the power-up state is ready to power up (state 1), the back-end power supply ≤ (front-end voltage +15V), lasts 50 ms;
(1) AND (2)) OR (3)

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (3s)
(1) The power-up state is a slow charging state (state 2), and the internal network heartbeat of the main drive circuit is updated normally when the fault is determined;
(2) The voltage difference between the front and rear ends of the main connection is less than 15V for 100 ms continuously;
(3) The front-end voltage is not sufficient for 100 ms continuously greater than the undervoltage point;
(1) AND (2) OR (3))

Reset conditions:
(1) Faults cannot be automatically recovered.
(2) If the power is turned on again after PowerDown and the fault entry conditions are not met, the fault exits.

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (3s)
(1) The detection function is turned on, and the power-on state is slow charging state 2;
(2) The internal network communication message heartbeat of the main circuit is normal;
(3) The slow charging contactor is closed for a period of time (depending on the voltage, the time varies);
(4) The back-end voltage of the slow charging contactor is still below a certain value (50V);
(1) AND (2) AND (3) AND (4)

Reset conditions:
(1) Faults cannot be automatically recovered.
(2) If the power is turned on again after PowerDown and the fault entry conditions are not met, the fault exits.

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (350ms)
(1) The detection function is turned on, and the power-on state is slow charging state 2;
