(1) AND (2) AND (3) AND (4)

Reset conditions:
(1) Faults cannot be automatically recovered.
(2) If the power is turned on again after PowerDown and the fault entry conditions are not met, the fault exits.

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (2ms)
(1) There is a power-on instruction;
(2) The power-on state is in progress;
(3) Not a one-click power-on and not a panel control
(4) TM speed greater than 500rpm 
(1) AND (2) AND (3) AND (4)

Reset conditions:
(1) There is an instruction to power off;
(2) The power on state is not currently being powered on;
(3) Switch on the electrical condition with one click;
(4) The rotation speed is less than 500rpm;
(1) OR (2) OR (3) OR (4)

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (2ms)
(1) The power-on state is ready to be powered on (state 1);
(2) The power-on state is ready to close the main connection (state 3);
(3) The KL30 voltage is less than the fault threshold (8.6V for 12V systems, 15.7V for 24V systems);
(1) OR (2)) ADN (3)

Reset conditions:
(1) The power-on state is ready to power on (state 1) or ready to close the main connection state (state 3);
(2) The KL30 voltage is greater than (fault threshold +1V); (8.6V for 12V systems, 15.7V for 24V systems);
(3) There is an instruction to power off;
(4) The circuit is powered up;
((1) AND (2)) OR (3) OR (4)

Maturation conditions: Trigger conditions: (2ms)
(1) There is a closing command and the power-on is completed;
(2) The absolute voltage difference between front-end voltage and back-end voltage continuously exceeds 20V for 50ms;
(3) Intranet communication failure without a loop;
(4) The KL30 voltage is below the fault threshold (6V for 12V systems, 12V for 24V systems).
(1) AND ((2) AND (3)) OR (4))

Reset conditions:
