troubleshoot_en:
Possible reasons: 1. The output current is too large;
2. The hall or detection circuit is disturbed or abnormal;
3. Hall is disconnected or abnormal;
4. Abnormal rotation signal. ; Maintenance advice: Check whether the motor is out of control;
Check whether the load is too large and the motor output current is too large;
Check the VCU torque request instructions;
Check whether the three-phase output cable is damaged;
Check whether the rotary cable is damaged;
If all of the above is normal, it is recommended to replace the controller.

