trigger_en:
Phase loss during operation: satisfies any of the operating conditions 1 or 2
Working condition 1:
 1) Enable output phase loss detection during operation (F10-17)
 2) Operating frequency > 0.8 Hz;
 3) The controller is in operation;
 4) Three-phase maximum current effective value/minimum current effective value ≥11, three-phase maximum current effective value > 12.2% base value current;
 5) Condition 4) Determined every 5 switching cycles, satisfied 5 times in a row, and a missing phase fault is reported.
Working condition 2:
 1) The output AC voltage is greater than the rated voltage & the effective value of the output AC current is less than 1/40 of the base value current,
 2) The operating frequency of the synchronous motor type is less than 1/4 of the rated frequency of the motor, and the asynchronous motor has no frequency requirements;
 3) If 1) and 2) are satisfied at the same time, the fault counter is +1; otherwise, -1; if the fault counter is greater than 10, a phase loss fault is reported.
Power-on phase loss detection: lasts 4 ms when all of the following conditions are met
 1) The controller is powered on at low voltage for the first time;
 2) When the tube is first opened, UV, VW, and WU three-phase pulses are sent separately for phase sequence phase loss detection.
PS: base current = Min (0.5 times the maximum current of the motor, 0.25 times the maximum current of the controller); diagnosis time: operating condition 1: strongly related to carrier frequency and output current size;
Working condition 2: Test once in 2ms;
Power-up output phase loss detection: 4ms

troubleshoot_en:
Possible reasons: 1. The three-phase output of the controller is out of phase;
2. Abnormal current detection. ; Maintenance advice: Check whether the motor is damaged;
Check the three-phase cable for damage or poor contact;
If all of the above is normal, it is recommended to replace the controller.

trigger_en:
1) The controller is in a shutdown state, and the reverse electric potential amplitude is less than 0.85 times the bus voltage;
2) Continuously sample the three-phase current 50 times (2 ms/time) and calculate the average value, greater than 15.6% of the AD full-scale current value;
3) Three consecutive tests meet the conditions and 2 report zero drift faults;
(1) & (2) & (3); Diagnosis time: 300ms

troubleshoot_en:
Possible reasons: 1. Rotation and disconnection;
2. The rotation interference is too large due to poor grounding, etc.;
3. Detect chip circuit abnormalities;
4. Abnormal motor rotation or excessive leakage current;; Maintenance suggestions: Check whether the rotation cable is damaged;
Check the grounding of the motor and controller;
Check whether the rotation impedance value of the motor is abnormal;
If all of the above is normal, it is recommended to replace the controller.

Possible reasons: 1. The battery power supply is working abnormally;
2. The battery detection circuit is abnormal. ; Maintenance advice: Check whether the battery voltage is too low;
Check whether the positive and negative wires of the control power supply in the controller are loose;
If all of the above is normal, it is recommended to replace the controller.

