(1) OR (2)

Entry conditions: PowerON; 1) Bus voltage < bus undervoltage fault trigger point: 560V (F10-01 setting) for 1 s;
2) Or, bus voltage < (bus undervoltage fault trigger point -100V)
3) Also, the operation instructions are valid;

Entry conditions: PowerON; phase loss during operation: satisfies any of the operating conditions 1 or 2
Working condition 1:
1) Enable output phase loss detection during operation (F10-17)
2) Operating frequency > 0.8 Hz;
3) The controller is in operation;
4) Three-phase maximum current effective value/minimum current effective value ≥11, three-phase maximum current effective value > 12.2% base value current;
5) Condition 4) Determined every 5 switching cycles, satisfied 5 times in a row, and a missing phase fault is reported.
Working condition 2:
1) The output AC voltage is greater than the rated voltage & the effective value of the output AC current is less than 1/40 of the base value current,
2) The operating frequency of the synchronous motor type is less than 1/4 of the rated frequency of the motor, and the asynchronous motor has no frequency requirements;
3) If 1) and 2) are satisfied at the same time, the fault counter is +1; otherwise, -1; if the fault counter is greater than 10, a phase loss fault is reported.
Power-on phase loss detection: lasts 4 ms when all of the following conditions are met
1) The controller is powered on at low voltage for the first time;
2) When the tube is first opened, UV, VW, and WU three-phase pulses are sent separately for phase sequence phase loss detection.
PS: base current = Min (0.5 times the maximum current of the motor, 0.25 times the maximum current of the controller)

Entry conditions: powerON; 1) The controller is shut down, and the reverse electric potential amplitude is less than 0.85 times the bus voltage;
2) Continuously sample the three-phase current 50 times (2 ms/time) and calculate the average value, greater than 15.6% of the AD full-scale current value;
3) Three consecutive tests meet the conditions and 2 report zero drift faults;

Entry conditions: PowerOn; 1) In the operating state;
2) Also, the motor speed exceeds 3500rpm (F10-12);
3) Also, lasts 100ms;
4) Also, overspeed fault detection enabled (F10-10)

Entry conditions: PowerON; 1) Speed control mode, and in operation;
2) Also, the motor's current rotation speed frequency and target speed frequency deviation deviation deviation detection threshold (F10-15);
3) Also, the deviation is too large and lasts more than 3s;
4) Also, enable detection of excessive speed deviation (F10-14)

Entry conditions: PowerOn; 1) In the operating state;
2) Frequency <1Hz
3) The current exceeds the rated value by 1.5 times;
4) Meet the above three conditions at the same time and maintain it for 10s;

Entry conditions: PowerON; 1) Module temperature ≥ module overtemperature reset point: 80℃ (F10-03), start power reduction;
2) Module temperature> module overheating point 85℃ (F10-02), power drop to 0;
3) Also, the controller overheats and reduces power, F10-04;

Entry conditions: powerON; 1) Motor temperature≥motor overheating reset point: 140℃ (F10-08), power reduction starts;
2) Motor temperature > motor overheating point 150℃ (F10-07), power drop to 0;
3) Also, the controller overheats and reduces power, F10-09;

Entry conditions: PowerOn; 1) In the operating state;
2) The motor speed exceeds the overspeed power reduction threshold (F10-13) and the power reduction starts;
3) The motor speed exceeds the overspeed detection threshold of 10,000 rpm (F10-12), and the power is reduced to 0;
4) Motor overspeed power reduction enabled, F10-11

Entry conditions: powerON; 1) The temperature sample value voltage is greater than the dropout detection threshold voltage:
PT1000 voltage threshold: 3.25V
PT100 voltage threshold: 3.25V
NTC voltage threshold: 3.08V
